{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310849,"nonce":"i6keUsaBe1DP7N7bWEHoXuqkE7s=","title":"MoE on 16GB: the blocker is nue's QUANT FLOOR (Q4_K), not MoE engineering. 35B-A3B needs \u003c=2.6 bpw and every such file throws at header ...","message":"**ASSESSED 2026-08-19 (11-agent workflow). Two load-bearing facts VERIFIED IN\nTREE by me, not taken on trust.**\n\n**1. THE QUANT FLOOR IS THE BLOCKER — HARD, VERIFIED.**\n`nue/nue/loader/GGUFReader.hx:186-200` `tensorByteSize` handles exactly EIGHT\ndtypes — 0 F32, 1 F16, 6 Q5_0, 7 Q5_1, 8 Q8_0, 12 Q4_K, 13 Q5_K, 14 Q6_K — and\n`case _: throw`. `rayzor-tensors/haxe/rayzor/ds/QScheme.hx` has exactly four\nmembers (INT8, Q4_K_M, Q6_K, Q8_0). **Q2_K is dtype 10, Q3_K is 11, IQ families\nare higher — all unreachable; such a file dies at HEADER PARSE.** nue's floor is\n~4.8 bpw.\n\nQwen3.5-35B-A3B fully resident needs **\u003c= 2.6 bpw** (11.5 GB x 8 / 35.47e9).\nEvery file at that rung (UD-IQ2_XXS 10.66 GB, UD-IQ2_M 11.39 GB, UD-Q2_K_XL\n12.16 GB) is unreadable today. **The \"viable path\" is currently unbuildable.**\nQ2_K/Q3_K are the only credible extension — same 256-element super-block\ngeometry the band kernel uses — but 16-element sub-blocks double the scale-lookup\nrate and Q3_K adds an hmask plane, against a kernel already ISSUE-bound at IPC\n3.26 ([[perf_q4_kernel_is_spill_bound_not_source_tunable]]). IQ2_* are\ncodebook-gather quants and do NOT ride this kernel at all.\n\n**2. THE WIRING BAND, VERIFIED.** `runtime/src/haxe_sys.rs:3115` `decide_mlock`:\n`len \u003e total/2` -\u003e false, and on macOS `len \u003e= total/8`. On 16 GiB that is a\n**[2.00, 8.00] GiB** pin band. A model above 8 GiB is NOT pinned and gets\nMADV_RANDOM — unpinned AND no read-ahead, the worst pair, and precisely the\n2x pressure cliff in [[perf_7b_busy_laptop_pressure_robustness]]. **4B and 8B\nQ4_K_M sit inside the band; 14B (8.91 GB) falls outside it.**\n\n**3. STREAMING IS A LATERAL MOVE, NOT A LOSS — and the popular arithmetic is\nwrong.** The \"384 fetches x 4 MB = 1536 MB/token\" figure describes Qwen3-30B-A3B\n(48 layers/128 experts), NOT the target. Qwen3.5-35B-A3B is 40 layers x top-8 =\n320 fetches x ~1.92 MB = **614 MB/token**, 2.35x less. Corrected, streaming gives\n~9-12 tok/s at ~55% residency and ~15-19 at 80% — against a dense 7B measuring\n**17.95-21.08 tok/s** quiet (`nue/bench/mistral/history.tsv`). Large subsystem,\nno throughput win, and macOS offers no eviction primitive to build the cache\nwith. Do not build it — but do not claim it was measured to lose.\n\n**4. THERE IS NO EFFICIENCY CUSHION.** mistral-7B streams ~4.26 GB/token at\n17.95-21.08 tok/s = **76-90 GB/s against a 95.1 GB/s ceiling — 80-94% of the\nmemory wall.** nue's dense Q4_K path is AT the wall; a smaller-tile MoE kernel\nstarts below it, not above.\n\n**5. WHAT SURVIVES — THE ACTUAL THESIS.** Sparsity at MATCHED Q4_K_M quality\ncuts per-token traffic from the dense 7B's 4.26 GB to **2.24 GB — 1.9x less\ntraffic for 5x the parameters**. No 2-bit gamble needed. It requires an MoE\ncheckpoint at **~18-20B total params** (what 11.5 GB buys at 4.83 bpw). **No\nQwen3.5 member exists at that size**; the available ones (Qwen1.5-MoE-A2.7B\n~14.3B, OLMoE-1B-7B ~6.9B) are engineering proofs, not products.\n\n**NOT VIABLE AT ANY EFFORT: Qwen3.5-122B-A10B.** 6.60 GB/token active — 1.5x\nMORE than a dense 7B. Ceiling 11-12 tok/s WITH INFINITE RAM. Its always-resident\ntrunk (4.83 GB) exceeds the whole Mistral-7B file.\n\n**THE DECIDING EXPERIMENT, BEFORE ANY nue CODE:** download\n`unsloth/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-GGUF` UD-Q2_K_XL (12.16 GB) and run it under\n**llama.cpp** on this box against Qwen2.5-7B-Q4_K_M. Record (1) PERPLEXITY on the\nsame corpus the gate uses — **there is zero published 2-bit quality evidence for\nthis family, and the whole bet is \"2.7-bit 35B-A3B beats 4.8-bit dense 7B\"**;\n(2) decode tok/s + ttft; (3) PEAK MEMORY FOOTPRINT via `time -l`\n([[reference_macos_peak_footprint_is_the_metric]]); (4) the TENSOR-TYPE\nHISTOGRAM, which IS the decoder list nue would have to implement — and if it\nmixes IQ types, the Q2_K path dies too. One afternoon, zero lines of nue code.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_moe_viability_quant_floor` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}